-- Conquest of Azeroth class trainers, the core every zone package builds on: one trainer kit per
-- CoA class (12-32), the stock class trainers turned into plain NPCs, Mathrengyl Bearwalker retitled
-- as the Darnassus Primalist, and the templates of the class-chain targets and credit markers that
-- several zones share. No creature is spawned or deleted here.
--
-- WHERE EACH VALUE COMES FROM
--   trainer spells  the Books of Ascension row builder (mod-spellbook BuildRows, window view) run over
--     the headers it reads: AscensionCompatData::ClassSpells, AscensionProgression::Ranks,
--     SpellbookOffer/Trainer/RankData, minus SpellbookTreeSpellData; ReqAbility1 is the rank below,
--     ReqLevel the level the book gates the row at. MoneyCost follows the realm's book cost setting:
--     spellbook.conf has Spellbook.Cost.Enable = 0 (the Books of Ascension teach free) and CoA's
--     captured trainer window shows cost 0, so every row is 0. To charge the book price list
--     (SpellbookCostData, without Spellbook.Cost.Multiplier) set BOOK_PRICES_CHARGED in gen_ct_core.py
--     and regenerate; trainer_spell prices are fixed rows and do not read the config at run time.
--     Identical to the static replica research/class-trainers/mech/trainer_rows_static.csv
--     (3732 rows). No row is a Talent.dbc spell; every SpellId and ReqAbility1 exists in Spell.dbc.
--     The runtime-only zero-cost CharacterAdvancement entries add no rows. The core hides four level-1
--     basics (Shoot, Throw, Dual Wield, Auto Shot) from CoA classes through SkillLineAbility, as the
--     research measured.
--   trainers  Type 0 (class), Requirement = the CoA class; the greeting follows the stock trainer line
--     (INFERRED). A zone package links its trainers with creature_default_trainer to 900000 + class.
--   gossip  one menu per class, 930000 + class: the class text for that class, the refusal for every
--     other class, and "I seek training as a <Class>." for that class only. Texts are SOURCED-CACHE
--     (npccache) where CoA had one in a voice any trainer of the class can speak; the cache stores
--     paragraph breaks as runs of four spaces, written here as $B$B. New texts in CoA's voice
--     (INFERRED): greetings 930012 Barbarian, 930015 Witch Hunter, 930016 Stormbringer, 930021 Ranger,
--     930024 Pyromancer, 930025 Cultist, 930026 Starcaller, 930027 Sun Cleric, 930028 Tinker, 930030
--     Reaper; refusal 930114 Felsworn.
--   stock class trainers  (user decision 2026-09-23) every stock class trainer in the starting zones and
--     capitals stays standing as a plain NPC: trainer flags off (npcflag & ~48), title blank as the CoA
--     creature cache shows it (Maginor Dumas and Zayus keep the rank titles "Master Mage" and "High
--     Priest" that the cache keeps), no default trainer, and the train / unlearn / dual-spec options gone from
--     the menus only they use. Menus shared with first-level-town trainers keep their options; the core
--     hides them without the trainer flag (PlayerGossip.cpp:61-62) and without a trainer
--     (Creature::CanResetTalents). Their quests, texts, addons and paths are untouched.
--   Mathrengyl Bearwalker  SOURCED-CACHE subname "Primalist" at his stock Darnassus post; he keeps his
--     quests and his Morrowgrain seed service in his own Primalist menu.
--   chain templates  fixed by the quests' RequiredNpcOrGo; names from Exiles or the quest text, looks
--     are stock stand-ins (INFERRED). The zone packages spawn them and own the scripts of their spawns.
--
-- Id blocks: trainer 900012-900032, gossip menu 930012-930032 and 930040, new npc_text 930012-930030 and
-- 930114.

